  "query_preview": "into Friday to highlight this threat.\n\nIf you are traveling to the coast for Thanksgiving, be aware of\nthe tidal flooding potential, and follow any directions from \nlocal officials. Things could change in the other direction \nthough, and stay firmly in moderate. Regardless, significant \ntidal flooding is expected. Minor to moderate tidal flooding \ncould continue with Thursday Night's high tide, hence why the \nCoastal Flood Watch extends through Thursday night. Some areas\nof minor coastal flooding could begin as early as the Wednesday\nmorning high tide, but the most significant tidal flooding will\noccur on Thursday. Thus, will hold off on issuing an advisories\nfor minor flooding, as these may soon be covered by warnings.\n\nFor the tidal Delaware River, east/northeast flow does not \nusually produce anything more than minor flooding. There will be\na fresh water component to the water levels there though, and a\nstrong southwest into Friday will not allow the river to drain.\nThus, widespread minor coastal flooding is forecast starting\nwith Thursday afternoon's high tide, and this may last through\nFriday. Similar to the Delaware River, east/northeast flow also\ndoes not usually produce notable flooding on the Eastern Shore\nof Chesapeake Bay. However, a surge wave will likely make its\nway north by late Thursday from the southern portion of the bay,\nand as the flow turns more south/southwesterly Thursday night\ninto Friday, this could result in some widespread minor coastal\nflooding along the Eastern Shore. Some guidance is close to \nmoderate flood stage, so we will continue to monitor this.",
